Sentiment Analysis of Amazon Reviews Using NLP

1. Introduction

Sentiment Analysis is a Natural Language Processing (NLP) technique used to identify and classify emotions expressed in textual data. It helps businesses understand customer opinions, satisfaction levels, and market trends by analyzing reviews and feedback.

In this project, real Amazon customer reviews are analyzed using Python and the TextBlob library. The system classifies reviews into Positive, Negative, and Neutral sentiments. Visualizations such as bar charts, pie charts, and word clouds are generated to present the results effectively.

2. Objectives
Perform sentiment analysis on Amazon customer reviews.
Classify reviews into Positive, Negative, and Neutral categories.
Analyze public opinion through customer feedback.
Visualize sentiment distribution using graphs.
Generate business insights from customer opinions.

3. Dataset

The project uses the Amazon Review Polarity Dataset, which contains real customer reviews collected from Amazon.

Dataset Features:

Customer review title
Customer review text
Sentiment label
Large-scale real-world review data
